<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95162" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκορπιο-ειδής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>scorpion-like</i>, only in
			form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκορπιώδης</span> (q.v.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκορπιοειδές, τό</span>, <i>scorpion-wort</i>
			 (so called because of the like ness of
			its seed to a scorpion's tail), <i>Scorpiurus sulcata</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				4.192
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκορπίουρος</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
